Modified for BenCode:

- src/display_link.rs (MonoCode's recovery for a stalled display link,
  commits 189d64a0, c341daf6): a shared `CVDisplayLink` CoreVideo stopped
  behind the registry's back is started again (`CVDisplayLinkIsRunning`); a
  start is a failure only when the link really is stopped. macOS 14 and later
  pace frames with a `CAMetalDisplayLink` instead, so this serves macOS 12-13.
- src/window.rs (MonoCode be06a810): starting frames counts the active app's
  main or key window as visible whatever its occlusion state says
  (`is_frontmost`), so a synchronous redraw while AppKit briefly reports it
  hidden (a screenshot thumbnail dropped onto it) no longer leaves it without
  frames until something resizes it.
- src/window.rs, src/window/native_views.rs: BenCode's cutouts for native
  views layered behind the GPUI view (`hole_punch_marker` in
  vendor/gpui-pre-apple): `draw` collects them from the scene (`cutouts`),
  `hitTest:` passes pointer events through their unobstructed parts
  (`cutout_passes_through`), and `resetCursorRects` leaves them to the
  native view's own cursors.

BenCode 0.3.10 also watched for frames that stopped (`watch_frames`) and
yielded to AppKit's redraws during a live resize; 0.3.14's Metal display link
wakes on GPUI's frame waker and draws into the drawables it hands out, so
those are gone.

Everything else is the crates.io source unchanged. To move to a new
gpui-pre, copy its `gpui-pre-macos` here and carry those changes over.
